From 886295596805cf259ae9b80f0db6198fee657ea6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z0cal <gabriel_zocal@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:58:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] EvalMod: the even series behind PC_EM_EVEN (bts.em_even):
 degree 7 in z = 2 (y - 1/64)^2 - 1, then the 5 double angles

The shipped target (2 pi)^(-1/32) cos(2 pi (16 y - 0.25) / 32) is even in w = y - 1/64, so it is a Chebyshev series
of half the degree in z = 2 w^2 - 1: a constant add, one square (its x2 and -1 in the relinearization's epilogue),
a degree-7 series (PS k = 3, m = 2) and the shipped double angles. Depth 1 + PS(7) + 5 = 10 = PS(14) + 5: the
same output level, degree and scale bit for bit on n32, n32a4 and n32sp at every input top the shipped series
builds at, so no landing, plan or key changes.

- pc-core: EVALMOD_EVEN_CHEB (minimax of the final, double-angled error on |I| <= 15, |delta| <= 2^-4,
  sequential LP; perseus-speedrun scripts/em_even7.py) and EVALMOD_EVEN_SHIFT.
- pc-shadow: PsPlan::even_shift (serde default None), PsPlan::evalmod_even / evalmod_k16, build_even_prestep in
  build_evalmod_opts. Tests: plan shape, landing equality on three chains (lean and FIDESlib builders), op census,
  and an exact RNS interpreter of the program on constant polynomials: shipped 27.40 bits (reproduced), even 29.53.
- pc-gpu: BtsSetup::evalmod_even (+ evalmod_ps), SparseBCfg::em_even (K = 16 only); dense / StC-first / SparseB
  build from it. pc-py session: cfg.bts.em_even. pc-bench bts / bts --all / stcf-prec: PC_EM_EVEN=1.
- pc-config: field bts.em_even (PC_EM_EVEN, kernel switch); field counts 270 / 362.

n32sp, top 50, lean builder, fused program: products 11 -> 10, rescales 16 -> 14, weighted-sum terms 14 -> 7
(limbs 447 / 692 / 592 -> 400 / 596 / 295). Not measured on a GPU.

